        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Meena's grandmother said that too little of some nutrients makes us ill.\n\"What happens without vitamin C?\" Meena asked."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "deficiency",
          "vitamin",
          "hygiene"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Lack of a nutrient causes a deficiency disease. Lack of vitamin C causes scurvy, of vitamin D causes rickets, of iron causes anaemia and of iodine causes goitre.\nEating a balanced diet with fruits, vegetables, pulses, grains and milk prevents these.\nFood hygiene means washing hands, washing food, covering cooked food and storing it safely."
        }
